  "_about": "a mallard (coats: the drake, the hen) afloat (swim.depth: the waterline at y = .07 in its rest frame): a long boat of a body -- chestnut breast, vermiculated grey flanks, grey-brown back under the folded wings, black rump and curled tail coverts, white tail -- short neck with the white ring, glossy green head, flat yellow bill with its black nail; the hen (coat 1) mottled brown and buff all over, the dark crown and eye stripe, the orange bill with its dark saddle, the same blue speculum between white bars -- aloft (the viewer's fly) the folded wings turn into the body and a spread wing of its own swings out feather by feather (duck.py, nbwing.aloft): grey-brown coverts, the white bar, the blue speculum along the trailing edge, the long grey-brown primaries, pale beneath (2026-11-08, review.py) The bill-yellow `culmen` ell under the bill's root removed (it smeared yellow over the face round the horn bill).",
